e age in Mexico City</article-title><source>Contraception</source><year>2002</year><volume>66</volume><fpage>417</fpage><lpage>426</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12499034</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0010-7824(02)00410-9</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jackson</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Schwarz</surname><given-names>EB</given-names></name><name><surname>Freedman</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Darney</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Knowledge and willingness to use emergency contraception among low-income post-partum women</article-title><source>Contraception</source><year>2000</year><volume>61</volume><fpage>351</fpage><lpage>357</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10958877</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0010-7824(00)00117-7</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Spinnato</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Informed consent and the redefining of conception: a decision ill-conceived?</article-title><source>J Matern Fetal Med</source><year>1998</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>264</fpage><lpage>268</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9848690</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/(SICI)1520-6661(199811/12)7:6&#x0003c;264::AID-MFM2&#x0003e;3.0.CO;2-M</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Spinnato</surname><given-names>JA</given-names><suffix>2nd</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>Informed consent: are we there?</article-title><source>J Perinatol</source><year>1999</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>401</fpage><lpage>402</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10685267</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/sj.jp.7200249</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (ACOG)</collab></person-group><article-title>Using preimplantation embryos for research. ACOG Comittee Opinion No.   347.</article-title><source>Obstet Gynecol</source><year>2006</year><volume>108</volume><fpage>1305</fpage><lpage>17</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.acog.org/from_home/publications/ethics/co347.pdf"/><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17077265</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B31"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Instituto Nacional de Estad&#x000ed;stica (INE)</collab></person-group><article-title>Censo de Poblaci&#x000f3;n y Viviendas</article-title><year>2001</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.ine.es/censo2001/censo2001.htm"/></citation></ref><ref id="B32"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grady</surname><given-names>WR</given-names></name><name><surname>Klepinger</surname><given-names>DH</given-names></name><name><surname>Nelson-Wally</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Contraceptive characteristics: the perceptions and priorities of men and women</article-title><source>Fam Plann Perspect</source><year>1999</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>168</fpage><lpage>175</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10435215</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/2991589</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B33"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Steiner</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Dalebout</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Condon</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Dominik</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Trussell</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Understanding risk: a randomized controlled trial of communicating contraceptive effectiveness</article-title><source>Obstet Gynecol</source><year>2003</year><volume>102</volume><fpage>709</fpage><lpage>717</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14551000</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0029-7844(03)00662-8</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B34"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Trussell</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Jordan</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mechanism of action of emergency contraceptive pills</article-title><source>Contraception</source><year>2006</year><volume>74</volume><fpage>87</fpage><lpage>89</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16860044</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.contraception.2006.03.028</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B35"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mikolajczyk</surname><given-names>RT</given-names></name><name><surname>Stanford</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The empirical and ethical questions of   induced versus natural losses of preimplantation embryos</article-title><source>Contraception </source><year>2007</year><volume>in press</volume><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17434024</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.contraception.2006.12.006</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>